    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clītor</span></b> , ŏris,
			m., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clītŏrĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Arcadia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				35, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 6, 10, §
				20</span></i>.—<i>Abl.</i> Clitori, Nov. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 316, 5</span></i> (cf. Lachm. ad
				<i><span class="en">Lucr. 2, p. 49</span></i>): Clitore, Liv. l.
			l.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clītŏrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 15, 322</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 2, 13, § 16</span></i>
			.</div>
